# Purpose: Keep generated/private files out of version control.
# Interview Explanation: "Model weights and Python caches are deployment
# artifacts, not source code."
# Key Concepts: Git ignore patterns.
# Important Things to Remember: Keep the .prototxt/.caffemodel backups safe,
# but do not commit large model files unless your repository policy permits it.
# Dependencies: Git (optional).
# Why This File Exists: Prevents generated files and large model assets from
# being accidentally committed. Depends On: Git. Depended On By: Git only.
# Source: Standard Git ignore pattern.

venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
models/*.caffemodel
models/*.prototxt

# INTERVIEW NOTES: Ignoring files changes Git tracking, not runtime behavior.
